WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.767
-Tyler James.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.601
Do I call you Tyler James
or Tyler?

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.701
-Tyler is fine.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:06.133
My mother loves the James.
-She does.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:08.467
-She wants the whole full name
in there.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:09.968
-Yeah, it was great to see
your mom backstage.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.100
-Yeah, yeah.
-And your dad?

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.133
-Yeah.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:13.467
-They're very
supportive parents.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.467
-Very. I mean, in order
to be a child actor,

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:16.834
you need
really supportive parents.

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.601
You can't get to
the jobs by yourself.

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.434
-That's true, yeah.

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:23.067
Apparently, we met almost.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:24.534
-Yeah, yeah, yeah,

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:27.968
We met about 20 years ago
on "SNL."

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:31.801
We did a -- we did a sketch
that got cut last minute.

00:00:31.801 --> 00:00:34.801
I was 10, so I look
a little different.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.334
-Yeah.
I'm slightly taller

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:39.434
than I was the time,
but yeah, yeah, we did.

00:00:39.434 --> 00:00:41.634
-You have a picture here
of you and Tracy Morgan?

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:42.968
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.868
So I did a few sketches
on "SNL" at the time.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:48.367
That's the one with me
with Tracy.

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.701
That's in my mother's house,
by the way, so...

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.167
She framed it.
-She framed it,

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.167
it's sitting there.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:54.901
-Is my picture next to Tracy?

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:56.200
-It's going to be.
-It's going to be.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.601
-Oh, my God! Mom!
-It's gonna get the wall.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:58.934
You're gonna make the wall.
-Mom, you didn't hang me up?

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:00.133
I didn't make the wall?

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.400
-You're gonna now.
-You're going to now.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.167
-What a good guy Tracy is.
-Such a good dude.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:06.033
-He took care of me when I was
first on "SNL."

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.834
Like, barely, actually, when I
was first, he was like,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.200
"You want me show you the ropes?
Come on.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.734
You here with your dad?
Come and get in my limousine."

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.501
And we got in the back of his
limo, he take us to a party.

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:15.067
Like, he's the best guy.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.968
He was -- I remember him
being super respectful.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.734
He refused to curse around me
at the time.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.467
-Wow.
-Even in all the rehearsals.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:22.167
-That is so hard
for Tracy Morgan.

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.334
-I know. It's very, very hard.
-That's amazing.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:28.200
-Yes, yes.
-You got to get an experience

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.000
with one of your idols
at the Golden Globes.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.367
You won a Golden Globe.
First of all, congratulations.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.400
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.701
-You won a Golden Globe.
-I know.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.467
For the rest of your life,
you have that.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.834
-It's still setting in.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.901
-For the rest of your life,
that's part of your intro.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.667
-Yeah, yeah.
-Golden Globe winner.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.601
-I'm going to have them do that
at, like, dinner reservations.

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.534
-[ Laughs ] Everything.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:46.734
-Everything,
you have to say it.

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.601
-So you're at --
you're in the room.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:50.400
-I'm in the room --
-Actually, before the room.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:51.467
-I'm at the carpet,
right?

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.267
And they stop me
from going on the carpet,

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:55.033
and someone's cutting the line
and I'm, you know,

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:56.634
I'm about --
my ego's about to go off.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.501
But then it's Eddie Murphy,
and I'm like,

00:01:58.501 --> 00:01:59.634
well, yeah, that makes sense.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:01.133
That makes sense.
Yes, let him go.

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.200
And we have a brief moment
on the carpet.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.200
Someone says, Can you guys
take a photo together?

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.901
And I'm like, "That's completely
up to Eddie Murphy."

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:10.968
That's -- he gets to decide
that, and he was fine with it.

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.534
And that could --
the night

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.133
could have ended for me
right there.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.300
I would have been done at that.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.434
I had a photo with Eddie Murphy,
it's going to go

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:17.667
on my mother's wall.
I think it's already up.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.400
That's -- that was it.
-It's already on mom's wall.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.767
-It's already on mom's wall.
-You never met Eddie Murphy.

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:26.000
-I had seen him in passing.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.934
I just really wasn't aware
that he knew who I was,

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:30.200
to be completely honest
with you.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.701
-Really?
-Really. I just -- I don't know.

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:35.400
You don't imagine
somebody like Eddie Murphy

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.033
watching anything
that you would do.

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:39.200
-You idolize Eddie.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.501
-Yes, 100%.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:44.267
I think every -- every
Black actor who does comedy

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:46.234
is stealing from Eddie Murphy,

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:49.467
in the same way Black actors
who do drama

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:50.934
ultimately are stealing
from Sidney Poitier.

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:52.167
It's just a lot of, like,
heists.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:53.200
That's what we're doing
with our performances.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.467
-Every -- yeah.

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:55.934
Eddie Murphy is the --
he's the top.

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:58.534
-He's the golden standard, man.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:02:59.968
It doesn't get
any better than that.

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:02.000
-Yeah, and did he say anything
to you or...?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.467
-Silence.
-Yeah.

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:04.634
-That's the way Eddie is,
though.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:06.300
-He's cool guy, he's quiet.
-He's super cool.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.467
He's like --
-When it's time

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:08.801
to turn it on,
I'll turn it on.

00:03:08.801 --> 00:03:10.834
-He gave me a thumbs up.
Good enough for me.

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.334
-Thumbs up.
That's big for Eddie.

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.234
-That's good enough for me.
-Eddie doesn't do thumbs up.

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.901
-No. I got a thumbs up.
I could have gone home.

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:19.467
-Well, something even cooler
than thumbs up happened

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:20.767
to you from Eddie Murphy.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.934
You win, and you
didn't know this even.

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:25.033
You win, you did your speech.
-I had no idea.

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:26.100
-You did the whole thing.
You just, what?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.534
You just kind of zone out
and you leave.

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:29.434
-Okay. So when you get up there
and you win,

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:31.133
what no one tells you is that
the lights are really bright.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:32.667
-Please tell me what it's like.

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.701
I guess -- I guess I'll never
experience it.

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:40.434
I guess I'll never
experience it.

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:44.100
Please tell me when you win
an award what's it like.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.968
-It's coming.
-No, it's not.

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:48.133
It's going to happen.
I believe in you.

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:50.000
-You were great.
So, you're up there.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.868
-I'm up there,
lights are really bright, right.

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:53.534
So I can't really see anything.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.200
And I don't know,
people talk through that --

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.601
that award wrap it up thing,

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:57.767
because it starts blinking
immediately.

00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.067
It's distracting, yeah.
-It's really red

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:01.501
and it's anxiety inducing,
so I'm just trying

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:03.968
to get off of stage
as fast as I can.

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:06.834
And it wasn't till I got back
to my seat that there was

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:08.501
a bunch of text messages
of people saying,

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:10.234
"Eddie stood for you."

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.267
And I was like,
"What does that mean?"

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:13.334
It's like, What?

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:17.834
And then they sent me
the photo, and...

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.968
I'm still trying
to process this.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:22.167
Eddie Murphy gave you
a standing ovation.

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:25.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:27.200
Come on, that's --

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.434
that's what I'm talking about.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.467
-I still don't --
It still hasn't set in.

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:31.767
Like, I'm looking at that,
and I'm like,

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:34.934
Wow, Gerard really must have
done something great.

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:36.434
-[ Laughs ] That was for you.

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:38.534
-That couldn't have been
for me, and I --

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:40.767
So I spent the next three
or four days

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:41.767
after the Globes trying

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:43.334
to get in contact
with Eddie Murphy.

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:45.734
Say, hey, I didn't see you.
I'm so sorry.

00:04:45.734 --> 00:04:47.100
-Yeah.
-But you mean, like,

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.167
the world to me?

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:50.200
So I'm just now processing
the Globe

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.467
because I spent so much time
trying to process that.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.868
-Yeah, well, Eddie
usually watches the show.

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:57.634
So, Eddie, you did a good thing
right here.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:04:59.400
-Thank you.
-This guy loves you.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.234
Tyler, you're so great on
"Abbott Elementary."

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:07.701
-Thank you.
-It was the funniest show on TV.

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:08.868
It's so great.
-Thank you.

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:10.601
-Quinta Brunson, genius.
So good.

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.734
-The best.
-Great show.

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.834
Yes, it is a great,
great, funny show.

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.467
100% on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:17.934
You crush it.
You're so good.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.067
You're so funny on that.
-Thank you.

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:20.100
It just got announced,
got picked up

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.000
for a third season.
-Season three.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:26.667
-Are you --
do you get different reactions

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:29.601
from people on the street now
that you're on this hit show?

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:31.100
-[ Sighs ] Yes.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:35.834
So, I've been "famous"
for a lot of my life.

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:37.100
-Yeah.
-I started on the show

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.434
called "Everybody Hates Chris."

00:05:38.434 --> 00:05:41.100
That was about 15 years ago.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.534
Thank you.

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:44.934
So since then, I've had, like,

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:46.501
a lot of experiences
of seeing people

00:05:46.501 --> 00:05:49.901
try to figure out
what I'm from on the street.

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:51.767
-Okay.
-And depending on what

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:53.767
their face does,
I'll then know

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:55.400
because it's like
they hit, like, three seconds.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.000
I'm walking by them.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.434
You know, they have to --
the brain has to make

00:05:58.434 --> 00:06:00.200
all the connections.
-Yeah, moves very fast.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.601
-Very, very fast.

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:04.634
So now it's really fun to watch

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:07.234
and try to see
what people know me from

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:08.400
based on their reactions.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.667
-Give me an example.
-Okay.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.734
So, like, the face always
starts the same, right?

00:06:11.734 --> 00:06:13.200
It's always a...

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.734 --> 00:06:17.100
If it's "Everybody hates Chris,"

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.300
because I'm like
everybody's cousin, it's...

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:23.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.167 --> 00:06:26.968
You know, that's -- So I'm like,
yeah, yeah, from that.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:29.834
-Yeah, that's right.
-I did a show called

00:06:29.834 --> 00:06:31.868
"The Walking Dead" for a while.

00:06:31.868 --> 00:06:36.334
If it's that,
it'll be a...

00:06:36.334 --> 00:06:39.501
Because they just saw me die,
and I'm like it's okay, y'all.

00:06:39.501 --> 00:06:41.133
-I guess that's the reaction.

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.033
-The new one is fun.
-Oh.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:46.033
-It's...

00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:47.734
-Oh!

00:06:47.734 --> 00:06:49.000
It's oh, you just seen me on
"Abbott."

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.567
You think I'm sexy.
Thank you, I appreciate it.

00:06:50.567 --> 00:06:52.601
-That's what I'm talking about.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.601 --> 00:06:54.601
That's exactly right.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:54.601 --> 00:06:57.601
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here is Tyler James Williams

00:06:57.601 --> 00:06:59.534
in next week's episode
of "Abbott Elementary."

00:06:59.534 --> 00:07:01.033
Take a look at this.

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:02.501
-Gregory.
-Hmm.

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:05.934
-So, how's your relas going
with your student's parent?

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:07.634
-Worst possible
way to phrase that.

00:07:07.634 --> 00:07:09.400
Former students parent,
and it's going well.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.868
It's me and Amber's
first Valentine's Day,

00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:12.868
so I want to get it right.
Brought three gifts.

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:14.968
And I'm still trying to decide
which two to send back.

00:07:14.968 --> 00:07:16.567
-Oh, nail biter.

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:18.934
Well, I do fancy myself
quite the gift giver.

00:07:18.934 --> 00:07:19.968
So, if you need help, I --

00:07:19.968 --> 00:07:23.033
-No.
-Hello, everyone.

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:25.767
So I found this Valentine
in my mailbox.

00:07:25.767 --> 00:07:27.934
It's from,
"a secret admirer,"

00:07:27.934 --> 00:07:29.801
Candy heart with my name on it.

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:31.501
Is this from one of you guys?

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.767
-Tyler James Williams.

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:40.701
"Abbott Elementary" airs
Wednesdays at 9:00 P.M. on ABC.

